    "summary": "Fixed the missing-workflow bypass: authorizeApproval takes the workflow from meta.workflow, and for an artifact whose meta does not say reads it from the file-name prefix (DEF, HLD, LLD, PLAN), so a PLAN with no workflow in its meta is authorized like any plan; a test covers it (a nameless plan held by bob is refused and not stamped). On the scope remark: the optional subject parameter of TeamGateRefusedError and claimsEnforcedFor in gate.ts are s5's own file and are what this Task needs to name a Task in the refusal and to decide whether an unresolvable approval applies; no other Story's shared machinery was changed. gates.ts changes are the approval guard only. The earlier fixes stand.",
